project: java-grinder
target: java-grinder

# File-input (CLI) target: feed the fuzz bytes as a Java .class file to java_grinder — the tool that
# reads JVM bytecode and emits assembly for a retro CPU. The bytecode parser (common/JavaClass,
# common/JavaCompiler) and the per-platform code generator both run on the input. Not libFuzzer: the
# natural fuzz surface is the tool on a .class file, so the built ELF is its own reproducer. @@ is the
# input-file placeholder.
#
# Ported from the old integration's single target (old: /java_grinder @@ out amiga); the binary now
# lives at /mayhem/java_grinder. Args are <class> <outfile> <platform>: java_grinder reads @@ as the
# .class, writes the generated assembly to /tmp/out (discardable scratch), targeting the `amiga`
# platform. A valid .class compiles to exit 0 (passing test); malformed bytecode exercises the reader.
#
# The scratch output MUST be a writable path (/tmp, a tmpfs). Mayhem mounts the commit image rootfs
# READ-ONLY during dynamic-analysis/coverage collection, so an absolute output under the baked image
# dir (e.g. /mayhem/out) can't be opened -> java_grinder gets a NULL FILE* -> the sanitized build
# aborts (UBSan, Generator.cxx) on EVERY input -> 0 edges covered -> "Run Failed". The original wrote
# a RELATIVE `out` into Mayhem's writable working dir; /tmp/out is the explicit, robust equivalent.
cmds:
  - cmd: /mayhem/java_grinder @@ /tmp/out amiga
testsuite:
  - https://$MAYHEM_DOMAIN/$MAYHEM_PROJECT/$MAYHEM_TARGET/testsuite.tar
  - file://mayhem/java-grinder/testsuite
